# Session artifacts. Sessions are created under the directory you run from, so
# running one inside a checkout puts them here. Each workspace also writes its
# own self-ignoring .gitignore, but the root holds `current` and `history.json`
# and those must not be committed either: `current` is an absolute path on one
# machine, and a committed `history.json` would tell every fresh clone that
# questions it has never served were already used.
interview-sim-sessions/
sessions/
sim-sessions/
.sim/

# OS
.DS_Store

